1
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,399
The 7th Hachun City

2
00:00:30,399 --> 00:00:32,320
Primary School Essay Speech Contest

3
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:33,960
will begin shortly.

4
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,000
Please take your seats promptly.

5
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:22,400
Teacher, for the speech competition,

6
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:25,760
why do I have to read the essay you wrote?

7
00:01:27,879 --> 00:01:30,000
Didn't I tell you this already?

8
00:01:30,159 --> 00:01:31,120
Once you win the prize,

9
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:33,239
your classmates won't laugh at you anymore.

10
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,519
You'll be my pride,

11
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,040
the class's pride,

12
00:01:37,439 --> 00:01:38,760
the school's pride,

13
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:40,280
and your dad's pride.

14
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:41,560
Wouldn't that be great?

15
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:42,359
Right?

16
00:01:42,359 --> 00:01:44,640
But why do I have to read what you wrote?

17
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:45,560
You want to read your own?

18
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:46,120
Once we go back,

19
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,519
you can read it wherever you want.

20
00:01:47,519 --> 00:01:49,000
I want to read it right here.

21
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:51,959
The choice is yours.

22
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:53,560
I won't force you.

23
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:03,719
Don't be nervous.

24
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:06,879
I grant you strength.

25
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,360
Are you ready?

26
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:14,800
Go on.

27
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:27,599
Read mine!

28
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,879
Read mine!

29
00:02:34,759 --> 00:02:35,800
Next, please welcome

30
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:38,759
from Class 2, Grade 3 of Majiabao Elementary,

31
00:02:38,759 --> 00:02:40,120
Fang Haowen,

32
00:02:40,199 --> 00:02:42,319
to present his essay speech.

33
00:03:02,719 --> 00:03:04,159
My Father

34
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:40,959
Time for work! Time for work!

35
00:04:41,079 --> 00:04:42,120
Wake up, wage slaves!

36
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,720
Yours truly, Fang Haowen.

37
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,519
A mere drop in the vast ocean of literature.

38
00:04:47,759 --> 00:04:48,560
As a kid, I won

39
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:50,879
first place in the primary school speech contest.

40
00:04:51,199 --> 00:04:51,959
My lifelong dream

41
00:04:51,959 --> 00:04:55,000
is to publish a poetry collection that goes down in history.

42
00:04:55,439 --> 00:04:57,360
Writing tirelessly for over twenty years,

43
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,519
enduring hardships,

44
00:04:58,639 --> 00:04:59,639
and striving for success,

45
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:00,920
I finally squeezed my way into the city's

46
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:02,360
renowned Furong Group

47
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:04,040
to work at their subsidiary magazine,

48
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:06,360
becoming an enviable editor.

49
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:07,240
Fang Haowen!

50
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:08,480
Refill my water.

51
00:05:09,879 --> 00:05:10,639
Fang Haowen!

52
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:12,079
Pour me some coffee.

53
00:05:12,079 --> 00:05:12,639
Fang Haowen!

54
00:05:15,439 --> 00:05:16,759
I'm tired. Give me a hand.

55
00:05:17,399 --> 00:05:17,920
Fair enough.

56
00:05:18,279 --> 00:05:19,199
Even if my career

57
00:05:19,199 --> 00:05:20,199
is facing a little turbulence,

58
00:05:20,279 --> 00:05:21,240
my personal life

59
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:22,519
is still incredibly comfortable.

60
00:05:22,519 --> 00:05:23,279
Hey, buddy.

61
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:24,959
Put your arm down.

62
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:27,079
No, I want that kids' meal!

63
00:05:27,079 --> 00:05:28,360
I want it! I want it!

64
00:05:28,639 --> 00:05:29,399
You... Fine, fine, fine!

65
00:05:29,399 --> 00:05:30,160
A real man

66
00:05:30,439 --> 00:05:32,319
never bows down for a few bucks.

67
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:34,759
Can I still use this five-yuan voucher?

68
00:05:35,079 --> 00:05:35,639
Yes, you can.

69
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:39,120
Didn't you order this?

70
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:39,600
I'm not eating it.

71
00:05:39,959 --> 00:05:41,000
If you're not eating, let's go. We're going home.

72
00:05:42,839 --> 00:05:43,319
Let's go.

73
00:05:44,959 --> 00:05:45,920
I am but a humble man of letters.

74
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:51,000
"Who knows that the food on our plates

75
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:52,000
is earned with sweat, piece by piece."

76
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:56,519
I am also deeply involved in the real estate market.

77
00:05:57,079 --> 00:05:58,319
Your rent from last quarter

78
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:00,120
is already a full quarter overdue.

79
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:02,000
I told you he couldn't pay it.

80
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,759
Stop trying to be a writer.

81
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,920
"Writers" do nothing but sit at home all day.

82
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:07,680
At least go out and borrow some cash.

83
00:06:08,839 --> 00:06:09,959
You have one week.

84
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:12,639
After a week, I'll come help you pack up.

85
00:06:13,879 --> 00:06:14,600
Okay.

86
00:06:17,439 --> 00:06:18,199
But fortunately,

87
00:06:18,399 --> 00:06:19,399
I have a great roommate

88
00:06:19,399 --> 00:06:21,199
who shares my literary dreams

89
00:06:21,399 --> 00:06:23,240
walking this path with me.

90
00:06:24,959 --> 00:06:26,040
You should put your arm down too.

91
00:06:27,879 --> 00:06:28,720
Wang Fuxiang.

92
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:30,759
Also an editor at "Exquisite Living Guide."

93
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:32,319
He joined the magazine two years before me.

94
00:06:32,959 --> 00:06:34,920
He's my best friend in Huanxi City.

95
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:37,160
Dad.

96
00:06:38,839 --> 00:06:41,199
If we hadn't supported each other all these years,

97
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:43,920
we both probably would've moved back to our hometowns.

98
00:06:44,959 --> 00:06:46,160
When are you paying rent?

99
00:06:47,759 --> 00:06:49,319
Those two jerks left the lights on while they're out.

100
00:06:49,319 --> 00:06:50,480
Isn't that a waste of electricity?

101
00:06:54,759 --> 00:06:57,040
A little stress from life and work

102
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:59,040
only makes my words, during all-night writing sessions,

103
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:00,439
flow like a spring

104
00:07:00,439 --> 00:07:01,959
and my inspiration strike like an avalanche.

105
00:07:04,079 --> 00:07:05,360
Time for work! Time for work!

106
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:06,480
Wake up, you wage slaves!

107
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:10,319
Though I occasionally fail,

108
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,680
I keep fighting after every defeat.

109
00:07:14,079 --> 00:07:15,199
Oh God!

110
00:07:16,439 --> 00:07:19,040
Why did you... why?

111
00:07:19,759 --> 00:07:20,560
But I believe

112
00:07:20,879 --> 00:07:21,920
it's because they haven't been

113
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,879
seen by the truly talented.

114
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:28,720
Mr. Xia! Hello, Mr. Xia!

115
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,519
To become a writer like you

116
00:07:30,519 --> 00:07:31,639
is my lifelong dream!

117
00:07:31,639 --> 00:07:33,000
This is the manuscript of my poetry collection.

118
00:07:33,319 --> 00:07:34,480
Could you please give it a...

119
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:36,079
Alright, alright, alright, time's up.

120
00:07:36,079 --> 00:07:36,839
Let's go, Mr. Xia. Let's go.

121
00:07:36,839 --> 00:07:37,519
Mr. Xia, let's go.

122
00:07:39,879 --> 00:07:40,680
To publish my poetry collection,

123
00:07:41,079 --> 00:07:43,439
sometimes I resort to unorthodox methods.

124
00:07:43,439 --> 00:07:44,439
Hello, Mr. Xia.

125
00:07:44,439 --> 00:07:46,879
Could you spare a moment from your busy schedule

126
00:07:46,879 --> 00:07:47,959
to give me some pointers?

127
00:07:47,959 --> 00:07:48,720
In this stall.

128
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:49,680
Mr. Xia,

129
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,480
this is the manuscript of my poetry collection.

130
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:55,040
The paper is too stiff.

131
00:07:58,959 --> 00:08:00,040
I should've just used sandpaper.

132
00:08:00,639 --> 00:08:02,519
If you really want to publish your poems,

133
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,360
stop barking up the wrong tree.

134
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,319
Just win over Chief Editor Hao.

135
00:08:06,959 --> 00:08:08,279
Writing articles requires refinement.

136
00:08:08,279 --> 00:08:09,480
Refinement, and more refinement.

137
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:10,560
As for being a person,

138
00:08:10,839 --> 00:08:12,079
you must be upright, upright.

139
00:08:12,279 --> 00:08:12,759
Upright.

140
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:15,040
Sit, sit, sit.

141
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:18,639
Literary works like poetry,

142
00:08:18,639 --> 00:08:19,759
we've published them before.

143
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:21,000
No one buys them.

144
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:21,959
The stuff you write

145
00:08:21,959 --> 00:08:23,240
lacks a sense of reality.

146
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,079
You need to understand

147
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,040
the true, the good, and the beautiful.

148
00:08:26,759 --> 00:08:28,319
And you need to understand the false, the ugly, and the evil, right?

149
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:29,839
Hey bro, why are you looking at me?

150
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:31,600
You know, readers nowadays

151
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:33,919
are all after down-to-earth literature.

152
00:08:33,919 --> 00:08:34,399
Right?

153
00:08:34,399 --> 00:08:36,600
"Oh, the ocean is all water."

154
00:08:37,399 --> 00:08:38,799
"And the girls here"

155
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,639
"are all legs."

156
00:08:41,159 --> 00:08:42,039
If you write like that, it's very vivid.

157
00:08:42,039 --> 00:08:43,279
And he calls himself an intellectual?

158
00:08:43,279 --> 00:08:43,720
Great poem!

159
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:44,360
So disgusting.

160
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:44,879
Great poem!

161
00:08:44,879 --> 00:08:45,799
I'm willing to turn into soil for the flowers.

162
00:08:45,799 --> 00:08:47,480
When my dreams were disregarded,

163
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:52,000
my childhood sweetheart appeared before me.

164
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:07,480
Are you from Hachun?

165
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:08,919
Is your name...

166
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:09,360
Luna?

167
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:09,960
Wang Yue?

168
00:09:14,639 --> 00:09:15,159
You...

169
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:17,399
You're that guy from our class...

170
00:09:18,559 --> 00:09:21,159
Fang... Fang... Fang...

171
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,639
"My Father"

172
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:31,840
My father...

173
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:32,879
He can't read or write.

174
00:09:32,919 --> 00:09:34,759
But he is still very happy.

175
00:09:34,759 --> 00:09:36,720
His job is driving a cart.

176
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:37,919
Illiterate! Illiterate!

177
00:09:37,919 --> 00:09:38,519
You're illiterate!

178
00:09:38,519 --> 00:09:39,360
My dad is illiterate!

179
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:40,000
Haozi!

180
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:40,519
Right.

181
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:41,759
Haozi.

182
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:45,440
You still hit so hard.

183
00:09:49,399 --> 00:09:50,919
She was like a soft beam of light,

184
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:52,759
shining into my dreary life.

185
00:09:53,240 --> 00:09:55,000
Making those lonely nights of writing

186
00:09:55,159 --> 00:09:55,960
feel warm.

187
00:09:58,519 --> 00:09:59,399
How thoughtful.

188
00:10:00,159 --> 00:10:01,360
You look really sharp.

189
00:10:05,799 --> 00:10:07,240
Let's meet up again tonight.

190
00:10:08,679 --> 00:10:11,080
Hao Wenzhang, tell me what this is!

191
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:13,600
Why is it in your car? Speak!

192
00:10:14,799 --> 00:10:16,559
It's a shoulder pad for a trench coat.

193
00:10:16,559 --> 00:10:17,200
Bullshit!

194
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:18,360
This is a bra pad!

195
00:10:18,559 --> 00:10:19,360
You're shameless!

196
00:10:19,799 --> 00:10:20,639
Completely shameless!

197
00:10:20,759 --> 00:10:22,159
Don't pull my hair! Don't pull my hair!

198
00:10:22,399 --> 00:10:23,440
And you call yourself an intellectual?

199
00:10:23,919 --> 00:10:25,080
You're just a filthy pervert!

200
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:25,720
No, look...

201
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:26,679
Were you driving the car?

202
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:29,240
Was this bra pad found in your car?

203
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:30,480
Whose is it if not some slut's?

204
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:31,960
Tell me!

205
00:10:32,159 --> 00:10:33,279
Which slut is it?

206
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:35,320
I'm counting to three. Are you gonna talk?

207
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:36,039
You've got it wrong.

208
00:10:36,039 --> 00:10:36,799
You won't talk? Fine.

209
00:10:36,879 --> 00:10:38,000
Whose damn thing is this?

210
00:10:38,159 --> 00:10:39,080
When I catch you all,

211
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:40,000
you're all gonna die!

212
00:10:40,159 --> 00:10:40,759
Are you coming out or not?

213
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:41,960
They won't talk. You tell me!

214
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:42,840
You better tell me!

215
00:10:51,399 --> 00:10:53,559
If you really want to get your poetry book published,

216
00:10:53,759 --> 00:10:56,360
convince Chief Editor Hao.

217
00:10:59,559 --> 00:11:00,240
It's my fault.

218
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:05,559
It's really not that hard to talk about.

219
00:11:05,879 --> 00:11:06,639
Here's what happened.

220
00:11:08,039 --> 00:11:08,879
I recall that day,

221
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:12,039
I borrowed the Chief Editor's ride,

222
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:13,000
Right, right.

223
00:11:14,399 --> 00:11:15,519
and I gave a ride to a

224
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,759
long-time admirer of my poetry,

225
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:21,279
a young literary woman.

226
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,440
We had a great chat, really hit it off.

227
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:23,679
On certain viewpoints, we indeed

228
00:11:23,679 --> 00:11:24,559
inexplicably aligned.

229
00:11:24,559 --> 00:11:25,120
And then we...

230
00:11:27,919 --> 00:11:29,000
engaged in the joys of intimacy.

231
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:33,480
This is an absolute tit-al humiliation!

232
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:36,480
There are three things in life you never lend.

233
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,840
A car is second on the list.

234
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:40,120
I lent you the car, and that should've been that!

235
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,200
But you had to be in my car,

236
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:44,960
doing such a despicable thing!

237
00:11:45,159 --> 00:11:45,840
Let me tell you,

238
00:11:46,039 --> 00:11:47,080
I don't usually hit intellectuals.

239
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:47,639
Don't be mad, don't be mad.

240
00:11:47,639 --> 00:11:48,679
I really don't hit them.

241
00:11:48,679 --> 00:11:49,320
Haowen...

242
00:11:49,799 --> 00:11:50,919
Haowen knows he was wrong.

243
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,679
I've let myself down.

244
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:54,240
And you call yourself an intellectual!

245
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:55,279
Shameless!

246
00:11:57,039 --> 00:11:57,639
Does it hurt?

247
00:11:58,279 --> 00:11:58,879
No.

248
00:11:59,679 --> 00:12:02,320
From now on, we're brothers.

249
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:04,360
Starting today,

250
00:12:04,879 --> 00:12:06,320
your business is my business,

251
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:07,639
brother.

252
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:09,279
So, can you help me get published?

253
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,279
Chief Editor Hao?

254
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:21,039
Sorry for the trouble, sorry.

255
00:12:21,759 --> 00:12:22,399
Fang.

256
00:12:22,919 --> 00:12:24,039
I can't help you.

257
00:12:24,159 --> 00:12:26,279
But I'll introduce you to someone who can.

258
00:12:26,759 --> 00:12:28,879
She really likes us intellectuals.

259
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:30,840
Please, take a seat.

260
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:31,799
Okay, okay, okay.

261
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:32,960
Sit, sit, sit.

262
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:35,799
Is this the guy you said

263
00:12:35,799 --> 00:12:37,120
is super talented?

264
00:12:37,679 --> 00:12:38,759
To answer President Jin,

265
00:12:39,039 --> 00:12:40,320
President Jin is absolutely right.

266
00:12:40,559 --> 00:12:41,440
We've been through life and death together.

267
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:42,240
Brimming with talent,

268
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,159
and full of youthful spirit.

269
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:44,200
We're all friends here, sit and chat.

270
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:45,080
I wouldn't dare, I wouldn't dare.

271
00:12:45,399 --> 00:12:46,480
I am merely

272
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:49,639
a drop of water in the vast ocean of literature.

273
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:53,120
"A light skiff welcomes the honored guest,

274
00:12:54,519 --> 00:12:56,039
arriving across the serene lake.

275
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:58,679
Facing the pavilion with a cup of wine,

276
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:03,480
lotuses bloom all around."

277
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:10,679
Give us another one!

278
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:11,759
I wouldn't dare

279
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:12,600
show off anymore.

280
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:17,039
"Flowers fall, the tower empties, leaving emerald dust,

281
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:21,080
a thousand autumns of bright moon, sorrow forever new.

282
00:13:21,399 --> 00:13:24,159
On the plains in the west wind, all blossoms fade,

283
00:13:25,120 --> 00:13:27,039
save for the lotus alone,

284
